  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). View and edit an alignment of manuscript witnesses one character or word at a time, export it for tree-building software, then load the resulting NeXML tree to reconstruct ancestral (archetype) readings by parsimony and add them to the matrix. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
